WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.772 --> 00:00:08.731
<b>Your first match</b> – A guided tour on a test match, from Home to the match end. Nothing counts and nothing is sent.

2
00:00:08.781 --> 00:00:15.424
Home, the first time: “New here? Take the tour”. Tap “Start the tour”.

3
00:00:15.474 --> 00:00:23.060
<b>New match</b> – An official game. Signed in, the button reads “SV match” and you load the game from the Swiss Volley schedule;

4
00:00:23.110 --> 00:00:29.366
without an account the match stays on this device.

5
00:00:29.416 --> 00:00:34.432
<b>Test match</b> – Everything works, nothing counts. This walkthrough runs on a test match.

6
00:00:34.482 --> 00:00:39.864
<b>Easy match</b> – Just the score and shirt numbers: no rosters, no signatures.

7
00:00:39.914 --> 00:00:43.069
<b>Restore match</b> – Game number + game PIN:

8
00:00:43.119 --> 00:00:47.430
continue a match from another device, or bring one back.

9
00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:52.295
<b>Options</b> – Theme, the tap hints, point entry (rallies or continuous),

10
00:00:52.345 --> 00:00:55.865
effects and speed, the set 2-3 break.

11
00:00:55.915 --> 00:01:00.031
<b>? on every screen</b> – The help of that screen: short videos, answers and “Show me”.

12
00:01:00.081 --> 00:01:04.900
This walkthrough starts from there too.

13
00:01:04.950 --> 00:01:07.103
Chapter 2 of 8 · Match setup

14
00:01:07.153 --> 00:01:10.981
<b>Back / Scoresheet / Options</b> – Back to Home (the match stays there),

15
00:01:11.031 --> 00:01:14.653
the scoresheet preview, Options.

16
00:01:14.703 --> 00:01:20.422
<b>Match info</b> – “Load match from schedule” fills it from the Swiss Volley schedule;

17
00:01:20.472 --> 00:01:24.088
“Edit” changes it by hand.

18
00:01:24.138 --> 00:01:27.288
<b>The teams</b> – Each team: its name,

19
00:01:27.338 --> 00:01:32.369
shirt colour and the count of players, liberos and bench officials.

20
00:01:32.419 --> 00:01:35.574
<b>Coin toss</b> – Lights up when everything is complete.

21
00:01:35.624 --> 00:01:39.135
If it is grey, the yellow “!” tells you what is missing.

22
00:01:39.185 --> 00:01:42.479
<b>Edit roster</b> – Opens the team's roster.

23
00:01:42.529 --> 00:01:47.617
Tap it: the next chapter shows every way to get the roster in.

24
00:01:47.667 --> 00:01:49.858
Chapter 3 of 8 · Rosters: every way

25
00:01:49.908 --> 00:01:54.367
<b>Type the players</b> – Number, last name, first name, Licence/DoB, libero, C, then Add.

26
00:01:54.417 --> 00:01:58.036
The number can wait: the coin toss waits for it.

27
00:01:58.086 --> 00:02:01.247
<b>Upload PDF</b> – Roster import › “PDF”:

28
00:02:01.297 --> 00:02:06.019
the team's roster PDF or the Einsatzliste, from this device.

29
00:02:06.069 --> 00:02:10.643
<b>Photo of the list</b> – A photo of the printed Einsatzliste: the list's language first,

30
00:02:10.693 --> 00:02:15.696
then “Take a photo” or “Choose a picture”, set the corners, “Read the list”.

31
00:02:15.746 --> 00:02:20.563
The players go straight into the roster; the fields to check are marked there,

32
00:02:20.613 --> 00:02:25.768
and “Undo import” puts the roster back. Here nothing is photographed.

33
00:02:25.818 --> 00:02:30.527
<b>Remote</b> – The coach uploads the roster on roster.openvolley.app with your upload PIN,

34
00:02:30.577 --> 00:02:34.242
or sends it from the manager page.

35
00:02:34.292 --> 00:02:40.052
Tap “Remote” in “Roster import”: a demo upload is waiting.

36
00:02:40.102 --> 00:02:44.939
<b>Roster uploaded</b> – The uploaded roster with its players and bench officials.

37
00:02:44.989 --> 00:02:53.950
“Preview” shows it, “Accept” takes it, “Reject” puts it aside. Tap “Accept”.

38
00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:57.294
<b>Load saved team</b> – Signed in: a team of your account,

39
00:02:57.344 --> 00:03:02.208
with its players and their numbers.

40
00:03:02.258 --> 00:03:08.500
Here a demo team, nothing comes from a server. Tap “Load saved team”.

41
00:03:08.550 --> 00:03:16.499
<b>Pick the team</b> – Tap the demo team: it replaces the roster (the app asks first).

42
00:03:16.549 --> 00:03:20.237
<b>Add from club</b> – Signed in: your club's licence lists.

43
00:03:20.287 --> 00:03:24.521
Tap “Add from club”.

44
00:03:24.571 --> 00:03:27.975
<b>Your club's players</b> – Tick who plays, then add them.

45
00:03:28.025 --> 00:03:34.491
A player the saved team knows comes with the number; the others need one in the # field.

46
00:03:34.541 --> 00:03:41.721
The shield on a row shows who is on the club's lists.

47
00:03:41.771 --> 00:03:47.755
<b>Choose players</b> – Tick who plays from the players the app knows for this team, then “Use n players”.

48
00:03:47.805 --> 00:03:53.589
Tap “Choose players”.

49
00:03:53.639 --> 00:04:00.229
<b>The known players</b> – The list of known players: tick, untick, “All”.

50
00:04:00.279 --> 00:04:03.429
<b>Load TEST roster / Delete roster</b> – In a test match:

51
00:04:03.479 --> 00:04:08.110
made-up players to try everything. Delete roster empties the list.

52
00:04:08.160 --> 00:04:11.316
<b>More ways</b> – In Global mode the rosters come from Excel.

53
00:04:11.366 --> 00:04:17.276
A restored match brings its rosters, and during the match “Rosters” changes them.

54
00:04:17.326 --> 00:04:21.122
<b>Confirm</b> – Saves the roster and goes back to Match setup.

55
00:04:21.172 --> 00:04:26.389
“Back” leaves the roster as it was. Tap “Confirm”.

56
00:04:26.439 --> 00:04:28.626
Chapter 4 of 8 · Coin toss

57
00:04:28.676 --> 00:04:32.744
<b>Record the toss</b> – Which team is A (left) and who serves first:

58
00:04:32.794 --> 00:04:36.736
“Switch sides” and “Switch serve”.

59
00:04:36.786 --> 00:04:39.949
<b>Show roster</b> – Last changes: add or

60
00:04:39.999 --> 00:04:44.035
delete a player or a bench official.

61
00:04:44.085 --> 00:04:47.722
<b>Sign A / Sign B</b> – Captain and coach sign here,

62
00:04:47.772 --> 00:04:51.401
or later during the warm-up.

63
00:04:51.451 --> 00:04:55.240
<b>Confirm coin toss result</b> – Then the connection checks,

64
00:04:55.290 --> 00:05:00.329
and the scoring screen. Tap it.

65
00:05:00.379 --> 00:05:02.849
Chapter 5 of 8 · Set 1

66
00:05:02.899 --> 00:05:10.677
<b>Line-ups</b> – Enter both line-ups with the “Line-up A” and “Line-up B” buttons and choose the game captain.

67
00:05:10.727 --> 00:05:14.464
If you skip them, the walkthrough enters demo line-ups.

68
00:05:14.514 --> 00:05:17.669
<b>Start set / Start rally</b> – At the service whistle.

69
00:05:17.719 --> 00:05:24.845
The first one of a set reads “Start set” and asks for the set's start time. Tap it.

70
00:05:24.895 --> 00:05:30.578
<b>The point</b> – Tap the point button of the team that won the rally.

71
00:05:30.628 --> 00:05:36.363
<b>Time-out / Substitution</b> – Tap the box to record one.

72
00:05:36.413 --> 00:05:39.567
<b>The substitution dialog</b> – Who comes in, then who goes out:

73
00:05:39.617 --> 00:05:45.360
only legal players; several at once, then Confirm.

74
00:05:45.410 --> 00:05:48.846
<b>Improper request / Delay warning</b> – The team sanctions;

75
00:05:48.896 --> 00:05:52.509
the next ones show up here too.

76
00:05:52.559 --> 00:05:58.062
<b>A player</b> – Tap a player on court: substitution, libero, sanction, injury.

77
00:05:58.112 --> 00:06:02.281
<b>Decision change / Undo</b> – Give the point to the other team or

78
00:06:02.331 --> 00:06:07.658
replay it (the score before and after is shown), or undo.

79
00:06:07.708 --> 00:06:10.859
<b>Match</b> – Rosters, history, set preview,

80
00:06:10.909 --> 00:06:14.593
corrections, show on a scoreboard, stop the match…

81
00:06:14.643 --> 00:06:16.699
Chapter 6 of 8 · Set end · start of set 2

82
00:06:16.749 --> 00:06:20.391
<b>Set end</b> – At 25 with two points ahead the app ends the set:

83
00:06:20.441 --> 00:06:25.819
confirm the end time, or “Decision change” if the last point was wrong.

84
00:06:25.869 --> 00:06:32.296
The rest of the set got demo rallies. Tap “Confirm”.

85
00:06:32.346 --> 00:06:35.496
<b>Start of set 2</b> – The teams change sides:

86
00:06:35.546 --> 00:06:40.798
enter the new line-ups, then Start set. The break runs on the screen.

87
00:06:40.848 --> 00:06:42.352
Chapter 7 of 8 · Set 5

88
00:06:42.402 --> 00:06:48.798
<b>Skip to set 5</b> – Sets 2 to 4 get demo rallies, as if they were played (the scoresheet prints them), until it is 2:2.

89
00:06:48.848 --> 00:06:58.604
Then set 5 goes on live.

90
00:06:58.654 --> 00:07:02.718
<b>Before set 5</b> – A new coin toss for the deciding set: “Switch sides”,

91
00:07:02.768 --> 00:07:10.056
“Switch serve”, then confirm the set 5 setup. Tap the confirm button.

92
00:07:10.106 --> 00:07:14.137
<b>Court switch at 8</b> – In set 5 the teams change courts at 8 points:

93
00:07:14.187 --> 00:07:20.095
the app asks, the line-ups stay. Tap “Switch courts”.

94
00:07:20.145 --> 00:07:22.210
Chapter 8 of 8 · Match end

95
00:07:22.260 --> 00:07:27.440
<b>Match complete</b> – The winner, the results and the sanctions, as on the scoresheet.

96
00:07:27.490 --> 00:07:32.069
<b>Signatures</b> – The captains sign, then the scorers and the referees.

97
00:07:32.119 --> 00:07:36.609
A technical remark can be added for the administration.

98
00:07:36.659 --> 00:07:42.880
<b>Sign</b> – On the screen, or on the person's own phone.

99
00:07:42.930 --> 00:07:46.634
<b>Scoresheet</b> – Preview, print or save the scoresheet as a PDF.

100
00:07:46.684 --> 00:07:52.722
That's the whole match: well done.
